{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00712",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 13.28,
      "duration_seconds": 12.69,
      "text": "Good morning, dear. I do hope I'm not wasting your time, I only came because my daughter said I must, I keep forgetting my tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.81,
      "end_seconds": 23.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "You're not wasting it. Tell me how that happens, forgetting them. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.18,
      "end_seconds": 45.28,
      "duration_seconds": 20.1,
      "text": "Well, I have the morning ones and the evening ones, and in the morning I get distracted, there's the cat, and the radio, and the phone goes, and then at night I find the morning ones still on the saucer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.63,
      "end_seconds": 52.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "How often would you say you miss them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.36,
      "end_seconds": 69.09,
      "duration_seconds": 14.73,
      "text": "Oh, three or four mornings a week, I should think. I've written it on the calendar, but then I forget to look at the calendar!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.54,
      "end_seconds": 77.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "You're certainly not alone. Have you had any falls lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.25,
      "end_seconds": 85.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "No, no falls. I'm very careful with the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.24,
      "end_seconds": 89.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Any dizziness, light-headedness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.24,
      "end_seconds": 98.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "No, none. I'm steady as a rock, ask my daughter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.99,
      "end_seconds": 104.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Do you remember what the tablets are for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.95,
      "end_seconds": 115.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.54,
      "text": "They're for my blood pressure, the two of them. High blood pressure, I've had it since my fifties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.58,
      "end_seconds": 121.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Any allergies to medicines, that we should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.66,
      "end_seconds": 131.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.27,
      "text": "Penicillin. I came out in a rash, as a girl, and my mother said never again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.35,
      "end_seconds": 142.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Thank you. Let me check how you're doing. Pulse and pressure, please. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.55,
      "end_seconds": 146.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Take whatever you need. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.22,
      "end_seconds": 175.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.72,
      "text": "Pulse 68 and regular, blood pressure 148 over 84, temperature 36.5, oxygen 97 percent, weight 61 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.08,
      "end_seconds": 180.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Is that good, dear? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.63,
      "end_seconds": 192.3,
      "duration_seconds": 10.67,
      "text": "The pressure's a little high, which fits with missing doses. And your pulse is regular. Any breathlessness or chest tightness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.15,
      "end_seconds": 200.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "No, I walk to the shops and back without trouble."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.81,
      "end_seconds": 219.22,
      "duration_seconds": 16.41,
      "text": "That's good. Here's my thought. Two tablets, at two different times, is a lot to remember. I'd like to simplify it to one tablet, once a day. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.97,
      "end_seconds": 224.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "One! That would be lovely. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.58,
      "end_seconds": 236.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "I'm going to start you on ramipril, 5 mg once a day, for your blood pressure, and stop the other two."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.33,
      "end_seconds": 241.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "And the old ones? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.01,
      "end_seconds": 258.68,
      "duration_seconds": 15.67,
      "text": "The pharmacist will take them back. And we'll get a pill organiser, a box with the days of the week, so you can see at a glance."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.97,
      "end_seconds": 266.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Oh, like my husband's, God rest him. That was a good box. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.69,
      "end_seconds": 278.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "Exactly. Keep it by the kettle, so you see it when you make your morning tea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.61,
      "end_seconds": 284.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "The kettle. I never forget the kettle. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.14,
      "end_seconds": 298.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.43,
      "text": "I'd also like to check your kidney function with a blood test, since you're starting a new tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.72,
      "end_seconds": 305.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Of course. Can they do it today? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.36,
      "end_seconds": 322.18,
      "duration_seconds": 14.82,
      "text": "Yes, at reception. If you feel dizzy, or your face or lips swell, or you develop a dry cough that won't go, stop it and let us know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.96,
      "end_seconds": 328.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Right. I'll remember that. Or Maureen will. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.92,
      "end_seconds": 335.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Perfect. Thank you for coming in. ~"
    }
  ]
}
